{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass in the morning.</b> For the entire night she made herself out to be Rahel, by means of the three signs that her sister had transmitted to her — niddah and challah and lighting the lamp — just as Ya'akov had transmitted them to Rahel. Midrash: all night long the wedding guests were chanting: הא לייא הא לייא, and the next day, when he saw that she was Leah, he said: surely this is what they were chanting — הא לייא — hinting to me that she is Leah. He said to her: deceiver, daughter of a deceiver! At night I called you Rahel and you answered me; now I call you Leah and you answer me! She said to him: a man who has no pupils! Your father called you Esav and you answered him; he called you Ya'akov and you answered him — that is, from you I learned this deception, and your father answered through you, for he said: ״בא אחיך במרמה״. And from these matters Ya'akov began to hate her, as it is said: ״וירא ה' כי שנואה לאה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:19.035662918Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}